Corrected symbolic assumptions
------------------------------
The 08d verifier now declares exactly:

  n = sp.symbols("n", integer=True, nonnegative=True)
  delta = sp.symbols("delta", real=True)
  eps = sp.symbols("eps", positive=True)

The 08e verifier separately declares lambda>0 and epsilon>0.  No
nonnegativity assumption is imposed on delta; negative detuning is allowed.
All 08d identities and the order-one coefficient remain unchanged.

Exact displaced and Bogoliubov identities
------------------------------------------
Direct normal ordering and r^3+delta*r=eta give

 H/V=-3r^4/2-delta*r^2+(2r^2+delta)b_dagger b
 +(r^2/2)(b_dagger^2+b^2)-r O3+O4,

 O3=b_dagger^2 b+b_dagger b^2,
 O4=(1/2)b_dagger^2 b^2.

For A=2r^2+delta and Omega=sqrt(A^2-r^4), the selected real branch obeys

 C_lambda^2=(A/Omega+1)/2,
 S_lambda^2=(A/Omega-1)/2,
 2 C_lambda S_lambda=-r^2/Omega,
 C_lambda>0, S_lambda<0.

The anomalous coefficient cancels exactly:

 A C_lambda S_lambda
 +(r^2/2)(C_lambda^2+S_lambda^2)=0.

Writing C0=sqrt(1/2+1/sqrt(3)) and
S0=-sqrt(-1/2+1/sqrt(3)),

 C_lambda/C0 =
 1+delta(-1/3+sqrt(3)/6)lambda^2
 +delta^2(17/72-sqrt(3)/9)lambda^4+O(lambda^6),

 S_lambda/S0 =
 1+delta(-1/3-sqrt(3)/6)lambda^2
 +delta^2(17/72+sqrt(3)/9)lambda^4+O(lambda^6).

Recursive calculation
---------------------
For

 K(lambda)=lambda^2(H/V-E_vac^(2))
 =sum_(j=0)^4 lambda^j K_j+O(lambda^5),

 intermediate normalization gives

 kappa_q=<n|sum_(j=1)^q K_j psi_(q-j)>,

 <m|psi_q>=
 <m|sum_(j=1)^q (K_j-kappa_j)psi_(q-j)>/
 [sqrt(3)(n-m)], m != n.

Every reachable number state is retained.  The dictionaries of shifts at
orders 0 through 4 are:

 (0);
 (-3,-1,1,3);
 (-6,-4,-2,2,4,6);
 (-9,-7,-5,-3,-1,1,3,5,7,9);
 (-12,-10,-8,-6,-4,-2,2,4,6,8,10,12).

Forbidden negative states vanish through their annihilation factors.  Parity
is calculated rather than assumed:

 kappa_1=kappa_3=0.

The nonzero coefficients are

 kappa_2=2sqrt(3)delta*n/3-n^2/12-n/12-1/72,

 kappa_4=
 -sqrt(3)delta^2*n/18+delta*n^2/18-sqrt(3)delta*n/9
 +delta*n/18-sqrt(3)delta/18+13delta/108
 +5sqrt(3)n^3/1296-n^2/18+5sqrt(3)n^2/864
 -n/18+139sqrt(3)n/2592-5/108+67sqrt(3)/2592.

Independent finite-sum calculation
-----------------------------------
The second organization evaluates directly

 (K4)_nn
 +sum[(K1)_nk(K3)_kn+(K3)_nk(K1)_kn+(K2)_nk(K2)_kn]/D_k
 +the three K1-K1-K2 permutations over D_k D_l
 +the K1^4 sum over D_k D_l D_m
 -kappa_2 sum (K1)_nk(K1)_kn/D_k^2,

where D_k=sqrt(3)(n-k).  This includes:

1. lambda^2 and lambda^4 frequency corrections;
2. finite-r corrections to cubic vertices in K3;
3. finite-r corrections to quartic vertices in K4;
4. second-order V4^2;
5. all three normalized V3^2 V4 placements;
6. normalized V3^4;
7. the complete normalization subtraction.

All sums terminate by the ladder shifts.  Exact SymPy assertions verify

 recursive kappa_2 == explicit-sum kappa_2,
 recursive kappa_4 == explicit-sum kappa_4.

No expected coefficient is inserted into either calculation.

Conversion from r to eta
------------------------
With epsilon=eta^(-1/3),

 r=epsilon^-1-(delta/3)epsilon+(delta^3/81)epsilon^5+O(epsilon^7).

Substitution verifies r^3+delta*r=epsilon^-3+O(epsilon^5).  The physical
energy is first assembled as

 E_n/V=E_vac^(2)+r^2[sqrt(3)n+lambda^2 kappa_2
 +lambda^4 kappa_4]+O(r^-4),

 and only then re-expanded in epsilon.

The exact quadratic contribution at eta^(-2/3) is re-derived as

 delta^3/27+sqrt(3)delta^2*n/18-delta^2/9
 +sqrt(3)delta^2/36.

Final coefficient and energy
----------------------------

 K_n(delta)=1/2592 times

 96delta^3+(144sqrt(3)n-288+72sqrt(3))delta^2
 +(144n^2-288sqrt(3)n+144n-144sqrt(3)+312)delta
 +10sqrt(3)n^3+(15sqrt(3)-144)n^2
 +(139sqrt(3)-144)n+67sqrt(3)-120.

Thus

 E_n/V=-3eta^(4/3)/2
 +[delta+sqrt(3)(n+1/2)-1]eta^(2/3)
 +delta(1-2delta)/6-(6n^2+6n+1)/72
 +K_n(delta)eta^(-2/3)+O(eta^(-4/3)).

The order-one coefficient from 08d is unchanged.

Spacing and second difference
-----------------------------
The coefficient of eta^(-2/3) in the spacing is

 L_n(delta)=1/1296 times

 72sqrt(3)delta^2+(144n-144sqrt(3)+144)delta
 +15sqrt(3)n^2+(30sqrt(3)-144)n+82sqrt(3)-144.

Therefore

 (E_(n+1)-E_n)/V=sqrt(3)eta^(2/3)-(n+1)/6
 +L_n(delta)eta^(-2/3)+O(eta^(-4/3)).

The second-difference coefficient is

 M_n(delta)=[48delta+10sqrt(3)n+15sqrt(3)-48]/432,

 so

 (E_(n+2)-2E_(n+1)+E_n)/V=-1/6
 +M_n(delta)eta^(-2/3)+O(eta^(-4/3)).

